---
import Text from "@/components/fundations/elements/Text.astro";
import Button from "@/components/fundations/elements/Button.astro";
import Wrapper from "@/components/fundations/containers/Wrapper.astro";
---

<section class="border-t border-base-800/50">
  <Wrapper variant="standard" class="py-20 lg:py-24">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-12 lg:gap-16">
      {/* Mascot image */}
      <div class="flex items-start justify-center lg:justify-start">
        <img
          src="https://cdn.hob.farm/pages/home/hob-mascot.jpg"
          alt="The Hob, HobFarm's resident maker"
          width="360"
          height="360"
          class="rounded-lg border border-base-800"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>

      {/* Main content */}
      <div class="lg:col-span-2">
        <Text tag="span" variant="textSM" class="text-accent-500 font-mono tracking-wider uppercase">
          Meet the Hob
        </Text>
        <Text tag="h2" variant="displayLG" class="mt-4 text-white font-display">
          The Hob
        </Text>
        <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
          <Text tag="p" variant="textBase" class="text-base-400 text-pretty leading-relaxed">
            In the folklore of the North York Moors, a hob is a household spirit.
            Not mischievous like elves, not menacing like boggarts. Helpful. A hob
            shows up uninvited, does the work nobody asked for, and disappears
            before dawn. Churns the butter, mends the fence, finishes the half-done
            chores. You never see it work. You just see the results.
          </Text>
          <Text tag="p" variant="textBase" class="text-base-400 text-pretty leading-relaxed">
            That's the idea behind HobFarm. The "farm" part pulls triple duty:
            a farm full of hobs tending to creative tasks, a server farm running
            autonomous workflows, and the folklore tradition of leaving offerings
            so the spirits keep working. Feed the system good inputs, and the
            hobs do the rest.
          </Text>
        </div>

        {/* Character description */}
        <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-base-800/50">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
            <div class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-accent-500"></div>
            <Text tag="h3" variant="textSM" class="text-white font-mono">
              The Character
            </Text>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <Text tag="p" variant="textSM" class="text-base-400 text-pretty leading-relaxed">
              He's been a mechanic with grease on his hands and a server rack behind
              him. A noir detective under sodium lights. A medieval tinkerer soldering
              something that shouldn't exist yet. The setting changes; the face
              doesn't. That's the point.
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" variant="textSM" class="text-base-400 text-pretty leading-relaxed">
              The Hob is built entirely through prompt engineering and reference
              management, not fine-tuning or custom models. Same bone structure, same
              attitude, same presence, regardless of what world he lands in. That
              consistency is what StyleFusion is designed to produce, and the Hob is
              the longest-running proof that the system works.
            </Text>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8">
          <Button isLink size="sm" variant="muted" href="/about">
            About HobFarm &rarr;
          </Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Wrapper>
</section>
